.PP
The release also includes \f[CR]SHA256SUMS\f[R], the compressed manuals
\f[CR]kosh.1.zst\f[R] and \f[CR]kosh.5.zst\f[R], and the Bash completion
file \f[CR]kosh.bash\f[R].
Check your download against its entry in \f[CR]SHA256SUMS\f[R].
Run \f[CR]kosh \-\-version\f[R] to see the installed version.
.PP
On macOS, an existing Homebrew installation can be updated with
\f[CR]brew update && brew upgrade kosh\f[R].
.PP
The VS Code and Zed extensions download Koshka when it is missing from
\f[CR]PATH\f[R].
The Neovim plugin is available as \f[CR]kosh.nvim\f[R].
.SH GETTING STARTED
Start an interactive shell, run a command, or run a script with
arguments.
.IP
.EX
kosh
kosh \-c \[aq]printf \[dq]%s\[rs]n\[dq] hello\[aq]
kosh script.kosh argument
.EE
.PP
Check a script without running it, or format it to standard output.
.IP
.EX
kosh \-\-lint script.kosh
kosh \-\-format script.kosh
.EE
.PP
Add \f[CR]\-\-apply\f[R] to write the lint fixes or formatted result
back to the file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
kosh [options] [script [argument ...]]
kosh \-c command [argument ...]
kosh \-s [argument ...]
kosh \-\-lint [\-c command ...] [file ...]
kosh \-\-format [file]
kosh \-\-lint \-\-format [file]
kosh [\-\-lint] [\-\-format] \-\-apply file ...
kosh \-\-as\-language\-server
.EE
.SH KOSHKA FEATURES
.SS Moods
The \f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood is the default.
It enables strict checks and analysis and holds nounset, pipefail,
failglob, and extended arithmetic on and nullglob off.
\f[CR]set\f[R], \f[CR]shopt\f[R], and \f[CR]koshconf\f[R] reject any
other value of these with a hint to use
\f[CR]koshconf set mood bash\f[R], but accept the value already held, so
\f[CR]set \-euo pipefail\f[R] still runs.
Every other option can be toggled.
The \f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood also resolves bundled utilities as commands
after PATH.
.PP
The \f[CR]bash\f[R] mood accepts Bash extensions with analysis off by
default.
The \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] mood is Bash syntax with the POSIX option on,
and sources the Bash startup files.
The \f[CR]sh\f[R] mood follows dash.
In this manual the \f[CR]bash\f[R] and \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] moods are
the Bash moods, the \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] and \f[CR]sh\f[R] moods,
where the posix option is on, are the POSIX moods, and every mood other
than \f[CR]kosh\f[R] is a compatibility mood.
.PP
In the compatibility moods every Bash option can be toggled, and an
explicit \f[CR]set \-u\f[R], \f[CR]set \-o pipefail\f[R],
\f[CR]shopt \-s failglob\f[R], or
\f[CR]koshconf set interpreter.arithmetic_uses_big_numbers\f[R] survives
a later change between them.
\f[CR]set \-o posix\f[R] selects \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R], and
\f[CR]set +o posix\f[R] selects \f[CR]bash\f[R] from the
\f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] or \f[CR]sh\f[R] mood.
.PP
The options whose defaults differ between the moods are these.
.PP
